## Phase 1, proof item 6: the same sphere at several RiTranslate offsets.
## Camera setup matches tests/rib/sphere.rib and corpus/menger.rib's
## convention (Translate 0 0 5 before WorldBegin). Three spheres, each in
## its own AttributeBegin/End block so their transforms don't compound,
## placed left, centre and right of the camera axis.
##
## Revert GMANTransform::apply to `return p;` (step 1) and every offset
## below collapses onto the same untransformed geometry: all three spheres
## render identically instead of at three distinct raster positions. See
## tests/transforms_test.cpp, which renders this file and asserts three
## separated silhouettes.
Display "transforms.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 300 100 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [90]
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
	AttributeBegin
		Translate -1.5 0 0
		Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
	AttributeEnd
	AttributeBegin
		Translate 0 0 0
		Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
	AttributeEnd
	AttributeBegin
		Translate 1.5 0 0
		Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
	AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
